PART 1 — DEFINITIONS

We work in a formal model of the extended ST-T1024 architecture. All definitions correspond to concrete objects in A1–A8.

Definition 1 (State Space S). The set of all reachable configurations of the agent at a single FSM step. Per A4, S is a finite product of finite domains (tile contexts, FSM state, bounded SRAM window, sensor quantization).

Definition 2 (Input Alphabet Σ). The set of distinguishable external signals arriving at the agent. Per A4 (as amended), Σ is a finite quantization of the world. Assumption of finiteness is an architectural decision, not an empirical observation.

Definition 3 (Action Library A). The ROM-burned set of actions. Per A2, A is finite, each action carries a schema ⟨id, type, preconditions, effects, envelope, cost⟩.

Definition 4 (Plan Library P). The ROM-burned set of plans. Per A3, P is finite, and each plan p ∈ P has a bounded maximum step count |p| ≤ K.

Definition 5 (Transition Function δ). δ : S × Σ → S. Per A1, δ is a deterministic function — not a relation. Same input, same state → same next state.

Definition 6 (Action Selection Function α). α : S → A ∪ {⊥, REFUSE}. Per A1 and A5, α is deterministic and total. ⊥ denotes "no action selected"; REFUSE denotes explicit refusal (0x-AMBIG-GOAL / 0x-UNSAFE-ACT).

Definition 7 (VERIFY Gate V). V : S × A → {PASS, FAIL}. Per A5, V is decidable in bounded time. The FSM cannot transition to COMMIT(a) unless V(s, a) = PASS.

Definition 8 (Envelope E). For each action a ∈ A, E(a) ⊆ S is the set of states from which a may be committed. Per A2, E(a) is declared in ROM. By construction of V, V(s, a) = PASS ⇒ s ∈ E(a).

Definition 9 (Trace τ). A trace is a finite sequence of steps: τ = ⟨(s₀, a₀), (s₁, a₁), …, (sₗ, aₗ)⟩ where sᵢ₊₁ = δ(sᵢ, σᵢ) and aᵢ = α(sᵢ). Length |τ| = l.

Definition 10 (Behavior Set B). B = {projection of every trace onto its action sequence} = {⟨a₀, a₁, …, aₗ⟩ : τ is a valid trace}. B is the object the theorem is about.

Definition 11 (Task-Level AET — T-AET). Per A0 §4.7, a maximum cycle budget T_max for any complete task. The FSM halts at T_max with 0x-BUDGET-EXCEEDED if not complete.

