PART 7 — TLA+ SKELETON

The following is a structural sketch, not a machine-checked specification. It defines the module, variables, and the shape of the theorem. Full specification, invariant definitions, and model-checking runs are the next step.

```tla
---------------------------- MODULE STT1024_Agentic ----------------------------
EXTENDS Naturals, FiniteSets, Sequences

CONSTANTS
    S,          \* Finite state space (A4)
    Sigma,      \* Finite input alphabet (A1)
    A,          \* Finite action library (A2)
    P,          \* Finite plan library (A3)
    K,          \* Max plan length (A3)
    D,          \* Max invocation depth (A6)
    T_max,      \* Task-level AET bound (A0 §4.7)
    delta,      \* S × Sigma → S, deterministic (A1)
    alpha,      \* S → A ∪ {REFUSE}, deterministic (A1, A5)
    V,          \* S × A → {PASS, FAIL}, decidable (A5)
    E           \* A → SUBSET S, envelope (A2)

ASSUMPTIONS
    FiniteS == IsFiniteSet(S)
    FiniteSigma == IsFiniteSet(Sigma)
    FiniteA == IsFiniteSet(A)
    FiniteP == IsFiniteSet(P)
    BoundedPlans == \A p \in P : Len(p) <= K
    BoundedDAG == D \in Nat /\ D > 0
    PositiveBudget == T_max \in Nat /\ T_max > 0

VARIABLES
    s,          \* Current state ∈ S
    cycles,     \* Accumulated cycle count
    trace,      \* Sequence of (state, action) pairs
    halted      \* Boolean — trace terminated

vars == <<s, cycles, trace, halted>>

Init ==
    /\ s = CHOOSE x \in S : TRUE    \* initial state
    /\ cycles = 0
    /\ trace = <<>>
    /\ halted = FALSE

\* One FSM step: select action, verify, commit or refuse.
Step ==
    /\ ~halted
    /\ LET a == alpha[s] IN
       \/ \* Commit path
          /\ a \in A
          /\ V[s, a] = "PASS"
          /\ trace' = Append(trace, <<s, a>>)
          /\ s' = delta[s, CHOOSE sig \in Sigma : TRUE]
          /\ cycles' = cycles + 1
          /\ halted' = (cycles + 1 >= T_max)
       \/ \* Refusal path
          /\ a = "REFUSE"
          /\ trace' = Append(trace, <<s, "REFUSE">>)
          /\ s' = s
          /\ cycles' = cycles + 1
          /\ halted' = TRUE

Next == Step

\* The theorem's object: the set of all action projections of reachable traces.
BehaviorSet ==
    { [i \in 1..Len(t) |-> t[i][2]] : t \in TraceSet }

\* TLA+ statement of the theorem (to be discharged by model-checking).
THEOREM VerifiableAgency ==
    /\ IsFiniteSet(BehaviorSet)                       \* Finiteness
    /\ \A b \in BehaviorSet :
         \A i \in DOMAIN b :                          \* Envelope compliance
             \E st \in S : st \in E[b[i]]

=============================================================================
```

The theorem statement at the bottom is what needs to be discharged. TLA+ and its model-checker (TLC) can verify it for specific instances of the constants. Full generality requires a proof assistant (Coq, Lean, Isabelle).

